1
00:02:28,876 --> 00:02:30,044
I'm sorry, Nico.

2
00:02:31,170 --> 00:02:32,838
But now, you know the real me.

3
00:02:32,963 --> 00:02:35,257
I'm Alyana Heartily Ferrer.

4
00:02:35,507 --> 00:02:36,091
Dead?

5
00:02:36,175 --> 00:02:37,843
How did that happen? He was...

6
00:02:37,968 --> 00:02:39,511
He was still so young.

7
00:02:39,511 --> 00:02:41,138
And he was perfectly healthy.

8
00:02:41,138 --> 00:02:42,556
He wasn't even sick.

9
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:46,977
I can take good care
of my daughter, Roswell.

10
00:02:48,312 --> 00:02:49,813
Young was still new, right?

11
00:02:49,813 --> 00:02:51,148
If another Mafia took him out,

12
00:02:51,482 --> 00:02:52,858
what would they
even gain from it?

13
00:02:52,900 --> 00:02:56,028
Boulstridge, keep an
eye on my wife's mother.

14
00:02:56,028 --> 00:02:56,570
Lerwick,

15
00:02:56,695 --> 00:02:59,490
investigate the Mafia group that
Kevin Alferez joined.

16
00:02:59,615 --> 00:03:00,157
Lee.

17
00:03:00,366 --> 00:03:03,702
Find out who the fuck is this
so-called guardian angel of my wife.

18
00:03:03,786 --> 00:03:04,745
And you, Lamperouge.

19
00:03:04,745 --> 00:03:05,913
Keep an eye on Yaji.

20
00:03:05,996 --> 00:03:06,937
What about me, Dong?

21
00:03:07,915 --> 00:03:08,914
What am I supposed to do?

22
00:03:10,601 --> 00:03:11,929
- What's that?
- Nothing.

23
00:03:13,003 --> 00:03:15,714
I'll give you 15 minutes to
memorize their background.

24
00:03:16,465 --> 00:03:17,066
Whoa.

25
00:03:17,091 --> 00:03:18,717
15 minutes? That's so fast.

26
00:03:18,801 --> 00:03:20,594
They look so cool, Dong.

27
00:03:21,011 --> 00:03:23,222
I'm going to eliminate
them one by one.

28
00:03:25,391 --> 00:03:27,643
Why are you showing me all this?

29
00:03:30,270 --> 00:03:31,313
Why do you think?

30
00:03:38,696 --> 00:03:41,615
Did the Yaji's have something
to do with Moo's death?

31
00:03:43,826 --> 00:03:44,952
I'm not yet sure.

32
00:03:46,203 --> 00:03:49,248
But they are the mafia,
Nico Jeisz Young was trying to join.

33
00:03:50,541 --> 00:03:52,209
So even if they didn't kill him,

34
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:54,878
they are still
responsible for him.

35
00:03:55,879 --> 00:03:58,215
His blood is on their hands.

36
00:04:02,386 --> 00:04:03,345
That's right.

37
00:04:05,180 --> 00:04:07,391
Someone has to answer
for what happened to Moo.

38
00:04:11,812 --> 00:04:14,523
Tomorrow, first
thing in the morning,

39
00:04:14,940 --> 00:04:16,859
you're gonna start
your real training.

40
00:04:18,402 --> 00:04:19,194
Really?

41
00:04:21,071 --> 00:04:22,906
This is for real now, Zeke?

42
00:04:23,699 --> 00:04:24,669
Okay.

43
00:04:25,367 --> 00:04:27,286
Does that mean I'll
become a Mafia too?

44
00:04:29,079 --> 00:04:30,789
I'm gonna be in the Mafia?

45
00:04:31,457 --> 00:04:32,416
Awesome!

46
00:04:36,336 --> 00:04:37,755
You already are one.

47
00:04:38,213 --> 00:04:39,339
Pew!

48
00:04:40,090 --> 00:04:41,091
Pew, pew!

49
00:04:42,051 --> 00:04:42,551
Psst!

50
00:04:43,093 --> 00:04:44,803
This is a robbery.
Hand over your wallet.

51
00:04:45,262 --> 00:04:46,096
Your wallet!

52
00:04:46,388 --> 00:04:47,222
Pew, pew!

53
00:04:51,435 --> 00:04:52,227
Sit down.

54
00:04:53,020 --> 00:04:54,063
I need a codename.

55
00:04:54,438 --> 00:04:56,106
- Eat.
- I wonder what my codename should be.

56
00:05:49,243 --> 00:05:49,993
Moo.

57
00:05:50,369 --> 00:05:51,328
Moo!

58
00:05:53,831 --> 00:05:55,666
Hey! Hi, Moo!

59
00:06:01,588 --> 00:06:02,965
Aww, so cute!

60
00:06:03,090 --> 00:06:04,466
Me or the puppy?

61
00:06:04,842 --> 00:06:05,509
Both.

62
00:06:06,677 --> 00:06:07,427
Moo!

63
00:06:08,053 --> 00:06:08,941
Moo.

64
00:06:10,439 --> 00:06:11,481
Sorry Moo.

65
00:06:12,599 --> 00:06:13,308
Moo?

66
00:06:15,561 --> 00:06:16,348
Moo!

67
00:06:17,563 --> 00:06:18,504
Moo!

68
00:06:21,191 --> 00:06:22,334
Moo!

69
00:06:22,359 --> 00:06:23,316
Moo!

70
00:06:23,986 --> 00:06:25,154
Moo!

71
00:06:26,405 --> 00:06:27,660
Hey, hey.

72
00:06:29,032 --> 00:06:29,950
Are you okay?

73
00:06:34,413 --> 00:06:35,038
Wife.

74
00:06:36,456 --> 00:06:39,626
Zeke, I dreamed about Moo.

75
00:06:42,337 --> 00:06:45,007
I still can't believe he's gone.

76
00:06:46,425 --> 00:06:47,301
And...

77
00:06:48,969 --> 00:06:50,888
in my dream, you were the...

78
00:06:52,306 --> 00:06:54,099
you were the one who shot him.

79
00:06:57,769 --> 00:06:59,771
But I know it wasn't you.

80
00:06:59,771 --> 00:07:01,523
because you'd never do that.

81
00:07:08,989 --> 00:07:10,657
I'm sorry, Zeke.

82
00:07:12,951 --> 00:07:13,994
Don't be sorry.

83
00:07:15,787 --> 00:07:16,663
I understand.

84
00:07:22,586 --> 00:07:24,546
Shh, that's enough.

85
00:07:32,846 --> 00:07:34,306
If you don't feel
up to training,

86
00:07:35,641 --> 00:07:37,059
you should get some rest.

87
00:07:38,477 --> 00:07:40,062
No, no.

88
00:07:41,063 --> 00:07:43,732
I have to train. I
have to get stronger.

89
00:07:45,442 --> 00:07:47,110
I have to get stronger for Moo.

90
00:07:47,110 --> 00:07:51,323
So when we find out
who did this to him,

91
00:07:52,241 --> 00:07:54,284
I'll be strong enough
to face them all.

92
00:07:56,536 --> 00:07:57,416
Alright.

93
00:08:01,458 --> 00:08:02,244
Huh.

94
00:08:03,085 --> 00:08:04,711
Wow, it's still so early.

95
00:08:06,797 --> 00:08:08,757
Did my school schedule change?

96
00:08:10,384 --> 00:08:12,886
Or can I just go back to sleep?

97
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:15,222
If you really want to train,

98
00:08:15,222 --> 00:08:17,641
you have to get up and
fix yourself in the morning.

99
00:08:18,183 --> 00:08:19,476
So you can get more done.

100
00:08:20,310 --> 00:08:22,396
Didn't you say you
wanted to learn everything?

101
00:08:23,522 --> 00:08:24,398
Yeah, but...

102
00:08:24,773 --> 00:08:27,734
Take a quick shower now,
I'll wait for you downstairs.

103
00:08:31,530 --> 00:08:32,406
I love you.

104
00:08:34,074 --> 00:08:35,242
I love you too.

105
00:08:50,632 --> 00:08:52,843
I should've just chosen to rest.

106
00:08:53,176 --> 00:08:54,761
Why'd I have to
get all dramatic?

107
00:09:02,394 --> 00:09:02,936
Left.

108
00:09:03,603 --> 00:09:04,271
Right, right.

109
00:09:06,189 --> 00:09:06,892
Knee.

110
00:09:07,316 --> 00:09:08,066
One more.

111
00:09:09,234 --> 00:09:10,095
Right hook.

112
00:09:10,652 --> 00:09:11,478
Left hook.

113
00:09:12,362 --> 00:09:13,259
Wait.

114
00:09:16,992 --> 00:09:17,837
What?

115
00:09:19,619 --> 00:09:20,954
Do you still want to continue?

116
00:09:22,456 --> 00:09:23,399
Can you keep going?

117
00:09:23,892 --> 00:09:25,208
Yeah, I can. Just wait.

118
00:09:26,808 --> 00:09:29,394
I'm doing this so I
can protect myself.

119
00:09:30,505 --> 00:09:31,882
And the people I love.

120
00:09:35,802 --> 00:09:36,720
Including me?

121
00:09:40,223 --> 00:09:41,683
Of course, including you.

122
00:09:44,811 --> 00:09:45,354
Good.

123
00:09:46,063 --> 00:09:46,938
10-minute break.

124
00:09:47,647 --> 00:09:49,775
Then, we'll proceed
to gun firing.

125
00:09:50,108 --> 00:09:50,776
Huh?

126
00:09:51,276 --> 00:09:51,902
Really?

127
00:09:52,527 --> 00:09:53,111
Whoa!

128
00:09:53,195 --> 00:09:54,196
Let's do it now.

129
00:09:54,196 --> 00:09:54,821
I'm ready.

130
00:09:55,197 --> 00:09:55,906
Relax.

131
00:09:56,198 --> 00:09:58,450
Let's wait once you've
regained your energy.

132
00:09:59,242 --> 00:10:00,369
Then, we'll continue.

133
00:10:10,087 --> 00:10:11,213
Ow!

134
00:10:11,588 --> 00:10:12,589
Quit pouting.

135
00:10:13,340 --> 00:10:14,424
You look like a duck.

136
00:10:16,071 --> 00:10:17,030
A duck?

137
00:10:21,014 --> 00:10:21,848
Does it hurt?

138
00:10:45,372 --> 00:10:46,473
Whoa!

139
00:10:46,498 --> 00:10:47,569
PDA!

140
00:10:48,831 --> 00:10:50,655
What the fuck do you
need, Lamperouge?

141
00:10:51,086 --> 00:10:52,212
It's about Yaji, boss.

142
00:11:00,470 --> 00:11:02,097
What's your update on Yaji?

143
00:11:02,889 --> 00:11:04,850
Have you found
their other members?

144
00:11:04,850 --> 00:11:05,642
Not yet, boss.

145
00:11:06,601 --> 00:11:07,519
Yaji?

146
00:11:13,150 --> 00:11:14,818
I'll let you know as soon
as Jacob updates me.

147
00:11:15,777 --> 00:11:17,654
Were the Yaji's behind what
happened to Moo?

148
00:11:18,655 --> 00:11:20,490
Do you know who killed him?

149
00:11:21,408 --> 00:11:22,701
Not yet, Ma'am Aemie.

150
00:11:23,577 --> 00:11:25,579
But I have a hunch
who Yaji's boss is.

151
00:11:25,871 --> 00:11:26,329
Who?

152
00:11:27,122 --> 00:11:28,081
Eiji Ferrer.

153
00:11:29,207 --> 00:11:31,960
But I still don't have enough information,
so I'm not completely sure yet.

154
00:11:33,795 --> 00:11:34,676
Eiji.

155
00:11:35,172 --> 00:11:36,355
Eiji Ferrer?

156
00:11:37,424 --> 00:11:38,402
You know him?

157
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:42,660
Zeke...

158
00:11:43,054 --> 00:11:44,639
He's Caileigh's dad.

159
00:11:45,599 --> 00:11:46,908
I—Impossible.

160
00:11:46,933 --> 00:11:47,851
Impossible.

161
00:11:48,226 --> 00:11:49,144
I told you.

162
00:11:49,644 --> 00:11:51,313
You cannot trust anyone.

163
00:11:52,439 --> 00:11:53,773
What's the plan, boss?

164
00:11:56,902 --> 00:11:58,403
She has a daughter, huh?

165
00:12:00,780 --> 00:12:01,664
Kill her.

166
00:12:06,369 --> 00:12:07,287
Zeke?

167
00:12:08,663 --> 00:12:09,748
What are you saying?

168
00:12:09,748 --> 00:12:11,711
You're talking about
killing my friend.

169
00:12:13,001 --> 00:12:15,712
And we're not even
sure he's Yaji's boss yet.

170
00:12:17,005 --> 00:12:19,132
Besides, Caileigh
Ferrer is adopted.

171
00:12:19,633 --> 00:12:23,303
And from what I've learned, Eiji
Ferrer and Caileigh aren't that close.

172
00:12:26,139 --> 00:12:27,516
Caileigh's adopted?

173
00:12:29,851 --> 00:12:30,894
Yes, Ma'am Aemie.

174
00:12:31,853 --> 00:12:33,855
So killing Caileigh would
probably be pointless.

175
00:12:34,064 --> 00:12:35,440
But we don't know

176
00:12:36,149 --> 00:12:38,235
how much she
already knows about us.

177
00:12:38,777 --> 00:12:39,903
Especially about Aemie.

178
00:12:44,115 --> 00:12:45,408
Wait, hold on.

179
00:12:46,701 --> 00:12:49,037
Do you even hear yourselves?

180
00:12:51,164 --> 00:12:53,166
You're talking about
killing my friend!

181
00:12:54,292 --> 00:12:55,877
You're going to kill my friend?

182
00:12:55,877 --> 00:12:57,546
She could be pretending
to be your friend.

183
00:12:57,879 --> 00:13:00,382
We don't know. She might already
be planning something against you.

184
00:13:00,882 --> 00:13:03,051
So if that's what it
takes to keep you safe,

185
00:13:03,385 --> 00:13:04,177
then yes.

186
00:13:04,177 --> 00:13:06,012
Is that really how
you think, Zeke?

187
00:13:06,805 --> 00:13:09,724
All you ever think about
is killing, killing, killing!

188
00:13:15,397 --> 00:13:17,524
One of my friends just died!

189
00:13:17,858 --> 00:13:19,734
And now you want
to kill another one?

190
00:13:23,530 --> 00:13:27,033
How are you any different from the
heartless people who did that to Moo?

191
00:13:30,829 --> 00:13:33,039
You're not laying a
finger on my friend.

192
00:13:34,666 --> 00:13:35,875
And that's final.

193
00:13:55,604 --> 00:13:56,605
Where's your boss?

194
00:13:56,730 --> 00:13:59,691
Uh, Ms. Stonehurst, Mr. Roswell
is not picking up his cellphone.

195
00:13:59,983 --> 00:14:00,859
I don't care!

196
00:14:00,859 --> 00:14:01,827
Call him again!

197
00:14:01,852 --> 00:14:03,478
Uh, yes, Ms. Stonehurst.

198
00:14:12,370 --> 00:14:14,414
What's that woman been
feeding you, Ezekiel?

199
00:14:15,790 --> 00:14:17,334
So not you.

200
00:14:30,472 --> 00:14:31,014
Why?

201
00:14:31,556 --> 00:14:32,515
Let's meet.

202
00:14:33,266 --> 00:14:34,100
Can we do it later?

203
00:14:34,726 --> 00:14:35,602
No.

204
00:14:35,602 --> 00:14:37,312
Let's meet now.

205
00:15:06,174 --> 00:15:08,843
Could they be the people
Auntie wanted me to meet?

206
00:15:22,774 --> 00:15:23,858
Excuse me, miss.

207
00:15:25,777 --> 00:15:27,070
Need someone to watch that with?

208
00:15:31,032 --> 00:15:32,609
If there are still tickets left.

209
00:15:33,284 --> 00:15:35,249
Look at how big
this production is.

210
00:15:35,787 --> 00:15:37,580
I'm sure it's already sold out.

211
00:15:38,665 --> 00:15:39,791
Leave it to me.

212
00:15:51,177 --> 00:15:52,303
What?!

213
00:16:00,687 --> 00:16:02,772
A-after flirting with—

214
00:16:03,523 --> 00:16:05,442
Charina, you're gonna apologize?

215
00:16:08,486 --> 00:16:09,821
Just play along.

216
00:16:11,156 --> 00:16:13,992
Baby, you know she's the
one who flirted with me, right?

217
00:16:14,200 --> 00:16:16,202
Besides, I didn't flirt with—

218
00:16:17,162 --> 00:16:19,372
Roselle! I'm sorry.

219
00:16:19,873 --> 00:16:20,890
Roselle?

220
00:16:20,915 --> 00:16:22,584
That's Charina. Look
at you, all confused.

221
00:16:22,584 --> 00:16:23,960
You have way too many girls.

222
00:16:25,978 --> 00:16:27,229
Baby.

223
00:16:28,631 --> 00:16:30,300
You know you're
the one I love, right?

224
00:16:31,718 --> 00:16:33,094
Don't be jealous, okay?

225
00:16:51,863 --> 00:16:52,685
Hey.

226
00:16:53,698 --> 00:16:54,513
Pervert!

227
00:16:58,203 --> 00:17:01,482
Since you keep coming
over here and acting all cute,

228
00:17:01,507 --> 00:17:02,717
you might as well
buy me coffee.

229
00:17:04,042 --> 00:17:05,668
But we don't even
know each other yet.

230
00:17:06,544 --> 00:17:07,497
I'm Shin.

231
00:17:08,171 --> 00:17:09,536
Can you treat me now?

232
00:17:13,885 --> 00:17:16,137
Why are you still standing
there? Go order already!

233
00:17:17,639 --> 00:17:18,818
Okay, baby.

234
00:17:23,645 --> 00:17:24,779
Hello, Auntie?

235
00:17:25,438 --> 00:17:27,106
Did you find the person
I asked you to tail?

236
00:17:28,233 --> 00:17:30,026
Yes, but there's
this annoying guy.

237
00:17:30,485 --> 00:17:31,318
Annoying?

238
00:17:31,903 --> 00:17:32,997
Yeah, but...

239
00:17:33,112 --> 00:17:35,865
Somehow, his nosy
ass actually helped.

240
00:17:36,699 --> 00:17:37,801
What's his name?

241
00:17:37,826 --> 00:17:39,953
I don't know, Auntie,
and I'm not interested.

242
00:17:39,953 --> 00:17:41,122
He's so annoying.

243
00:17:43,832 --> 00:17:45,041
Call me later, Auntie.

244
00:17:45,041 --> 00:17:46,459
Okay, I'm gonna go
deal with that idiot first.

245
00:17:47,168 --> 00:17:49,671
Okay, Mik. I'll call you later too.

246
00:18:04,811 --> 00:18:05,770
Let's talk.

247
00:18:30,545 --> 00:18:32,005
Were you the one
who did that to Young?

248
00:18:33,673 --> 00:18:34,588
No.

249
00:18:35,341 --> 00:18:37,176
I don't have the
guts to kill a man.

250
00:18:39,929 --> 00:18:42,849
Age really does
matter, doesn't it?

251
00:18:44,893 --> 00:18:47,729
Talking to you is
such a waste of time.

252
00:18:48,688 --> 00:18:50,231
What do you mean?

253
00:18:59,699 --> 00:19:01,743
Age does really matter.

254
00:19:02,285 --> 00:19:03,828
You're too young to surpass me.

255
00:19:17,675 --> 00:19:19,219
I'm not your enemy.

256
00:19:21,012 --> 00:19:22,305
Who are you?

257
00:19:24,724 --> 00:19:26,184
You guess.

258
00:19:46,496 --> 00:19:48,331
I didn't plan on buying for two.

259
00:19:49,832 --> 00:19:50,917
Then stop trying to act all handsome.

260
00:19:51,793 --> 00:19:52,740
But I am handsome.

261
00:19:55,880 --> 00:19:56,709
Wait,

262
00:19:57,465 --> 00:19:58,506
why are you here anyway?

263
00:19:59,175 --> 00:19:59,915
Why are

264
00:19:59,968 --> 00:20:01,469
you staring at those five men?

265
00:20:08,726 --> 00:20:10,478
I bet one of them is your ex.

266
00:20:11,020 --> 00:20:14,642
You're probably trying to make him jealous,
that's why you pulled that stunt earlier.

267
00:20:18,611 --> 00:20:20,931
And if you're gonna date someone,
at least don't pick an ugly one.

268
00:20:22,198 --> 00:20:24,361
Wow, you're not
exactly a looker yourself.

269
00:20:31,978 --> 00:20:33,688
What the hell?

270
00:20:34,711 --> 00:20:36,212
What are those two doing here?

271
00:20:39,966 --> 00:20:41,300
Why is Fiona here?

272
00:20:41,300 --> 00:20:42,861
Why is she with Lionhart?

273
00:20:44,887 --> 00:20:46,222
Hey, is something wrong?

274
00:20:47,101 --> 00:20:48,423
Who are they? Do you know them?

275
00:20:54,814 --> 00:20:58,943
Boss, Fiona and Lionhart
just met up with those five men.

276
00:21:00,820 --> 00:21:03,573
Okay, follow Lionhart.

277
